EXT. FLOATING MARKET ON A CLOUD - DAY

Stalls drift on white vapor. Bridges of braided mist. Lanterns shaped like fish. Far below, a patchwork of farmland.

SABLE, 20s, a thief in a patched coat, crouches behind a stall of enchanted fruit. Her partner, BRINDLE OKAFOR-LYNN, 30s, hairy-eared and cheerful, juggles three glowing apples. A merchant, MADAME ZEPHYRINE, 60s, sells wind in jars.

SABLE
(whispering)
Brindle, stop juggling the evidence.

BRINDLE
It's not evidence. It's snacks.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Customers! Two coins for a breeze!

SABLE
We do not have two coins.

BRINDLE
We have one and a half.

SABLE
We have none. I told you not to spend on the pie.

BRINDLE
It was a good pie.

SABLE
It was a pigeon with crust.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Last chance, my darlings!

Sable pops up. Smiles at the merchant. Slides a hand toward a jar.

SABLE
Madame, we heard you sell the finest sirocco on the cloud.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Only the finest.

BRINDLE
How fine?

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Fine enough to carry you to the moon.

SABLE
We'll take two.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
At two coins each?

SABLE
At half a coin each, since you're our favorite.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Child, don't flatter me.

SABLE
Flattery's all I've got.

Brindle drops an apple. It bounces across the stall, rolls off the edge, and falls through the cloud. All three watch it go.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
That was an apple of wisdom.

BRINDLE
We'll find another.

SABLE
We won't.

Madame Zephyrine sighs. She uncorks a jar. A soft wind swirls out, lifts Sable's hair, and tugs at Brindle's coat.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Free sample.

BRINDLE
She likes us.

SABLE
She pities us.

MADAME ZEPHYRINE
Both.

The wind rises. Sable and Brindle grab each other's arms. They lift an inch off the cloud. They rise slowly, laughing, up toward the lanterns.
